  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Suppose two planets (spherical in shape) of radii <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;but mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi>M</mi></math> respectively have a centre to centre separation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi>R</mi></math> as shown in the figure. A satellite of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is projected from the surface of the planet of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> directly towards the centre of the second planet. The minimum speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> required for the satellite to reach the surface of the second planet is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">M</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>, then the value of&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br />[Given : The two planets are fixed in their position]</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6d6ce075-2e07-4240-8c0d-4d740bb060b9-image.png\" style=\"width: 201px; height: 125px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e7810cc5-4ec9-4e30-9c27-fee6b6ff17b0-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 141px;\" /></p><p>Acceleration due to gravity will be zero at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> therefore,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mn>9</mn><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>Apply conservation of energy and consider velocity at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is zero.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mn>9</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mn>9</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">M</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
